      "writtenOn": "2025-09-29T21:20:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The new `atomic_try_cmpxchg` could fail because the other ID (not `old`) sharing the `atomic_t` (`sc-\u003eids`) has changed, unrelated to this `swap_cgroup_cmpxchg` call. In which case `swap_cgroup_cmpxchg` would fail when it did not before, without checking to see if the problem was due to the `old` ID or the other / second ID.\n\nThe caller is designed to deal with failures, so this isn\u0027t the end of the world, but can you fix that part? Probably easiest to check that `old` is in `old_ids` after a `atomic_try_cmpxchg` failure, and retry if it is / fail if it isn\u0027t. Blind retries might help, but I\u0027d rather not.\n\nBTW next KMI thaw is about a year from now on 6.12, but I don\u0027t think we\u0027ll be able remove this then. 6.18 won\u0027t have this charge moving code at all.",
      "parentUuid": "370b2b4f_f05f5e2d",
      "revId": "8e677e18c907dc9726ef4787f92e72066973ecda",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
